WorkflowRouter_onReport
  ├── when the contract is paused
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when the caller does not have the KEYSTONE_FORWARDER_ROLE
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when the metadata is shorter than 64 bytes
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when the metadata is longer than 64 bytes
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when the workflow ID is zero
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when the workflow name is zero
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when the workflow owner is zero
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when the workflow metadata does not match
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when the report is too short
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when the target chain selector does not match
  │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__InvalidReportDomain
  ├── when the target router does not match
  │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__InvalidReportDomain
  ├── when the observation timestamp is in the future
  │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__ReportFromFuture
  ├── when the report is older than 30 minutes
  │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__ReportExpired
  ├── when the report is exactly 30 minutes old
  │   └── it should succeed
  ├── when the selector is not allowlisted
  │   └── it should revert
  ├── when the vault call fails
  │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__CallFailed
  ├── when all conditions are met
  │   └── it should succeed
  ├── when the workflow is removed and re-registered with a different name and owner
  │   ├── when the selector is not re-added for the new registration
  │   │   └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__SelectorNotAllowlisted
  │   └── when the selector is re-added for the new registration
  │       └── it should succeed
  └── when the workflow is renamed to a different name and owner without going through removal
      └── when the selector is not re-added for the new registration
          └── it should revert with WorkflowRouter__SelectorNotAllowlisted
